\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come, let us anew
\par Our journey pursue,
\par Roll round with the year,
\par And never stand still 
\par till the Master appear.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. His adorable will
\par Let us gladly fulfil,
\par And our talents improve,
\par By the patience of hope 
\par and the labour of love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Our life is a dream
\par Our time as a stream
\par Glides swiftlt away,
\par And the fugitive moment
\par refuses to stay.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. The arrow is flown,
\par The moment is gone;
\par The millenial year
\par Rushes on to our view,
\par and eternity's here.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O that each in the day
\par Of His coming may say:
\par I have fought my way through,
\par I have finished the work 
\par Thou didst give me to do!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. O that each from his Lord
\par May receive the glad word:
\par Well and faithfully done;
\par Enter into My joy, 
\par and sit down on My throne!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

